  "description": "A short lesson to help you apply Interoception: The Sixth Sense of Emotion.",
  "is_free": false,
  "published": true,
  "story": {
    "hook": {
      "text": "Your heart races, your stomach tightens, your breath quickens. The insula reads all of it and tells you how you feel.",
      "visual": "💓"
    },
    "buildup": {
      "text": "Interoception is the perception of internal body states: heartbeat, hunger, temperature, muscle tension, and more.",
      "visual": "🌡️"
    },
    "discovery": {
      "text": "The insula acts as the primary hub for interoception, mapping body signals and feeding them into emotional awareness.",
      "visual": "🗺️"
    },
    "twist": {
      "text": "People with higher interoceptive accuracy experience emotions more intensely and make better intuitive decisions.",
      "visual": "🎯"
    },
    "climax": {
      "text": "Alexithymia, the inability to identify emotions, is linked to reduced insula activity and poor interoceptive awareness.",
      "visual": "😶"
    },
    "punchline": {
      "text": "The insula makes connection.",
      "visual": "🔗"
    }
  },
  "quiz": {
    "question": "What is interoception?",
    "options": [
      "The perception of internal body states like heartbeat and hunger",
      "The ability to see in complete darkness",
      "The process of forming long-term memories"
    ],
    "correct": 0
  },
